Stand!

270
00:31:53.703 --> 00:31:54.662
Skip it.

271
00:32:05.924 --> 00:32:07.133
Get out everyone.

272
00:32:31.699 --> 00:32:32.617
Gi Jun.

273
00:32:36.079 --> 00:32:37.288
I'm begging you, aren't you...

274
00:32:40.083 --> 00:32:41.334
can't stop?

275
00:32:44.212 --> 00:32:45.505
I haven't heard in a long time

276
00:32:46.798 --> 00:32:48.091
such a tone from you.

277
00:32:50.134 --> 00:32:51.219
I'm asking you...

278
00:32:53.429 --> 00:32:55.807
like an old friend, in remembrance of the past.

279
00:32:57.767 --> 00:32:58.643
stop

280
00:33:03.272 --> 00:33:05.483
Clear. That's what I thought.

281
00:33:11.572 --> 00:33:12.490
Come on.

282
00:33:13.992 --> 00:33:15.201
I will spend

283
00:33:59.495 --> 00:34:02.665
I'm just doing my job.

284
00:34:03.791 --> 00:34:04.709
Do you understand?

285
00:34:37.533 --> 00:34:38.367
Nothing.

286
00:34:44.665 --> 00:34:46.876
Go and finish what you started.

287
00:34:51.547 --> 00:34:52.381
OK.

288
00:34:55.051 --> 00:34:56.135
See you soon.

289
00:36:08.916 --> 00:36:11.043
Well, how do you like sitting in this chair?

290
00:36:14.172 --> 00:36:15.923
you did it all

291
00:36:17.341 --> 00:36:19.844
just to sit right here, right?

292
00:36:21.387 --> 00:36:22.471
I don't know.

293
00:36:24.223 --> 00:36:27.185
It's not as great as I thought it would be.

294
00:36:28.477 --> 00:36:30.897
I've done a lot of shit to be here.

295
00:36:31.397 --> 00:36:33.232
If I had known that it was all in vain...

296
00:36:36.694 --> 00:36:37.904
Everyone thinks so.

297
00:36:38.779 --> 00:36:40.823
They are ready for anything for the sake of this chair.

298
00:36:42.867 --> 00:36:44.368
And when they get it,

299
00:36:45.244 --> 00:36:46.621
emptiness remains.

300
00:36:48.789 --> 00:36:52.335
Because there is only one way - down.

301
00:36:53.586 --> 00:36:56.923
To hell with it. This is just your opinion.

302
00:36:59.425 --> 00:37:00.635
But me?

303
00:37:00.718 --> 00:37:03.596
I enjoy the fight itself.

304
00:37:05.139 --> 00:37:07.225
I enjoy the tension before the battle

305
00:37:07.767 --> 00:37:11.103
and with every hit.

306
00:37:12.396 --> 00:37:16.359
And the best feeling was after the victory.

307
00:37:17.401 --> 00:37:19.946
The way my friends looked at me.

308
00:37:21.989 --> 00:37:23.282
my father

309
00:37:23.866 --> 00:37:27.328
I've probably felt that way all my life.

310
00:37:27.411 --> 00:37:28.621
I was so jealous of him.

311
00:37:30.122 --> 00:37:32.875
Respect. Delight.

312
00:37:37.880 --> 00:37:38.714
This is…

313
00:37:40.508 --> 00:37:42.510
This is not admiration or respect.

314
00:37:44.428 --> 00:37:45.721
This is fear.

315
00:37:47.431 --> 00:37:48.849
And he becomes a burden.

316
00:37:54.188 --> 00:37:55.314
And Mr. Chairman...

317
00:37:57.775 --> 00:38:00.111
probably didn't want you to carry this burden

318
00:38:01.195 --> 00:38:02.530
because he knew how it hurts.

319
00:38:02.613 --> 00:38:05.199
Enough talking about my late father.

320
00:38:06.617 --> 00:38:09.412
That's what I'm interested in

321
00:38:09.495 --> 00:38:11.289
because I really don't understand.

322
00:38:12.039 --> 00:38:15.042
Why go so far? Ha?

323
00:38:15.126 --> 00:38:19.005
why are you doing this
even though so much time has passed?

324
00:38:20.131 --> 00:38:22.758
Blyaha, you
gave up everything and ran away.

325
00:38:24.593 --> 00:38:26.679
Because it all started because of me.

326
00:38:28.306 --> 00:38:30.766
And through me, Gi Seok…

327
00:38:35.062 --> 00:38:37.273
Yes, because it works in this business.

328
00:38:44.655 --> 00:38:46.407
If you have already entered...

329
00:38:49.201 --> 00:38:50.328
you will not leave alive.

330
00:38:50.411 --> 00:38:51.245
No need.

331
00:38:51.996 --> 00:38:53.497
But what the hell!

332
00:38:53.581 --> 00:38:56.667
I said that it is not necessary!

333
00:39:17.605 --> 00:39:19.815
Well, shoot.

334
00:39:29.075 --> 00:39:30.659
My father was right.

335
00:39:32.536 --> 00:39:33.496
he said

336
00:39:34.538 --> 00:39:36.791
that you all live with nightmares every day.

337
00:39:38.084 --> 00:39:41.504
Why did I go in where I shouldn't have?

338
00:39:46.592 --> 00:39:47.426
And yet...

339
00:39:50.137 --> 00:39:53.391
Thank you for listening to me.

340
00:40:11.075 --> 00:40:11.909
Badge!

341
00:40:11.992 --> 00:40:12.993
You…

342
00:40:14.787 --> 00:40:16.622
you won't die that way.

343
00:40:36.725 --> 00:40:37.560
Ah...

344
00:40:39.562 --> 00:40:40.771
beg for forgiveness

345
00:40:44.108 --> 00:40:47.486
don't tell me
what to do, shitty scumbag.

346
00:42:07.316 --> 00:42:09.276
<i>I kept thinking: well, who will come here?</i>

347
00:42:13.030 --> 00:42:14.240
<i>But it's not bad here.</i>

348
00:42:17.993 --> 00:42:18.827
Hello brother.

349
00:42:21.121 --> 00:42:24.041
Maybe I should move.
Leave everything behind.

350
00:42:26.877 --> 00:42:27.711
Of course.

351
00:42:28.504 --> 00:42:30.881
It would be good. Drop everything and move.

352
00:42:31.507 --> 00:42:33.968
We will manage the campsite together.

353
00:42:38.055 --> 00:42:39.431
What is wrong with you?

354
00:44:05.517 --> 00:44:08.812
WITHOUT MERCY

355
00:47:00.108 --> 00:47:05.113
Translation of subtitles: Olga Tsiatska

